-- ── Pre-registered design decisions D1–D12 (the four open questions of the
--    phase spec + the calls they force; each is a claim round-010 must verify) ──

-- D1 (spec Q1 — physical encoding of supersedes(aid_new, aid_old)).
-- A supersedes fact persists as a RESERVED NODE RECORD inside today's closed
-- {nodes, edges} segment vocabulary:
--   NodeRecordV2 { id: fid(main, "supersedes", tuple), node_type: "$supersedes",
--                  file: "$rofl/supersedes", name: "", semantic_id: "",
--                  content_hash: 0,
--                  metadata: {"aid_new": <32-hex>, "aid_old": <32-hex>,
--                             "_source": author, "_generation": tick} }
-- written through the NEW additive derived commit path (v3 segments, D4).
-- Rationale with evidence: the edge encoding is FORBIDDEN by the P2 wont_fix —
-- multi_shard.rs upsert_edges (:506-529) SILENTLY SKIPS edges whose src is not
-- in node_to_shard, and an aid is not a node id, so the truth source would be
-- silently lost. record id = fid makes record identity ≡ fact identity (merge
-- dedup can never lose a distinct supersedes fact). The reserved file routes
-- every supersedes record to one shard and can never intersect a reanalysis
-- changed_files set.
-- LEGACY-VIEW VISIBILITY RULE (pre-registered, differential-pinned): reserved
-- "$supersedes" records ARE visible to the legacy node surfaces (node_count_at,
-- find_nodes_at, get_node_at) as ordinary rows — §9.4's `rows` semantics; they
-- are NEVER projected as node/type/attr FACTS (they project ONLY as supersedes
-- facts). Post-supersession differential: node-fact count == node_count_at
-- minus the reserved-record count; no attr/type leakage.
-- Forgery guard: a node GROUP asserting node_type "$supersedes" through
-- assert_batch bypasses the supersession boundary and is rejected E-SUP-001.

-- D2 (spec Q2 — first component of a scope-kill supersedes fact).
-- x := aid(aid_old, author_name, at_tick) — reuse of the aid() combinator with
-- the victim aid in the fid slot: deterministic, unique per (victim, author,
-- tick), content-derived, and the supersede assertion's own author/tick remain
-- recoverable from the record's _source/_generation (audit trail). This is a
-- per-victim id, a deliberate refinement of the spec's per-operation
-- recommendation (recorded honestly here): §2.4's liveness rule only ever
-- consults the SECOND component, so c0 is an identifier, not a join target.

-- D3 (spec Q3 — divergence-abort channel for E-SUP-001's second arm).
-- Option (b): contractual panic whose message carries "E-SUP-001", from
-- live_filter AND canonical_state_sha, on an assertion with
-- tx_invalidated != TX_OPEN that has NO live supersedes(_, aid) in the same
-- snapshot (precedent: canonical_state_sha's foreign-snapshot panic,
-- facts/mod.rs:539-546 doc). live_filter's signature is UNCHANGED. The doc's
-- literal E-SUP-001 (line ~330) is only the tick check; the divergence arm is
-- the phase brief's addition — recorded here as a P4 interpretation. P2's
-- silent rule-1 drop test (live_filter_passes_all_p2_rows_and_drops_tx_invalidated)
-- is UPDATED accordingly (silent-drop was P2 semantics; P4 aborts).

-- D4 (spec Q4 — multi-assertion coexistence through the write path).
-- Facts-layer writes (assert_batch AND supersede) go through a NEW additive
-- derived commit path: MultiShardStore::commit_batch_derived — records carry
-- DerivedFields and flush as v3 (FORMAT_VERSION_DERIVED) segments via a new
-- Shard::flush_derived_with_ids that mirrors flush_with_ids with add_derived
-- and bypasses the WriteBuffer entirely. One AssertBatch = one (author, tick)
-- = one commit = its own L0 segments, so coexisting authors land in separate
-- segments by construction; within one batch, same-record-key dedup (last
-- wins) reproduces WriteBuffer semantics and is same-aid M1 territory (P7).
-- The LEGACY write path (commit_batch/commit_batch_ext, WriteBuffer,
-- flush_with_ids, tombstones, ManifestEdit shape, checkpoints) is UNTOUCHED —
-- that is what keeps crash_recovery.rs out of this round's diff.

-- D5 (spec Q5 — author/tick physical carriers). author stays metadata _source,
-- tick stays metadata _generation (the Q2-synthesis inverse); facts-written v3
-- records duplicate tick into ProvenanceV2.generation and leave
-- rule_ast_hash = 0 (the u32 keeps its rule/plugin meaning for derive-written
-- segments; it is NOT repurposed as an AuthorId — a persisted author interner
-- is catalog-in-manifest work, P6).

-- D6 (spec Q6 — no cache writes). P4 writes NO tx_invalidated cache; every
-- written assertion carries TX_OPEN and liveness is paid as the honest
-- anti-join (§2.4 named cost; §5.6 assigns cache materialization to P7's
-- checkpoint mechanism). Cold cost on a supersedes-free base stays ~0: the
-- projection of "$supersedes" is a type-filtered scan pruned by the node_type
-- zone maps.

-- D7 (round-007-pre C9 — aid canonicalization, forced now). aid() changes to
-- hash the canonical author NAME (len-prefixed UTF-8): aid = BLAKE3(fid ‖
-- varint(|name|) ‖ name ‖ tick_le)[0..16] LE. Reason: supersedes fact tuples
-- now HASH aids into fids (canonical artifacts), and §9.2 forbids interned
-- u32s in canonical artifacts (process/declaration-order dependent — the
-- cross-process sha gate would fail). The §2.2 `author_u32` form is read as
-- the physical shorthand; recorded as a P4 interpretation. The P2 unit test
-- aid_depends_on_all_three_components is updated to the name-keyed signature.

-- D8 (grouping rule / C22-R1 reversal boundary). FactRow multi-assertion is
-- real for records in v3 (derived-column) segments: the projection groups all
-- live record versions by fid; distinct (author, tick) versions coexist as
-- assertions; same-(author, tick) re-asserts stay newest-wins (M1 dedup is
-- P7). Records in v2 segments KEEP the P2 winner-collapse (newest record per
-- record key, C22/R1) — forced by soundness: base v2 merges stay newest-wins
-- (crash/legacy path untouched), so a v2 multi-author projection would change
-- the canonical sha across compact(), violating C3 physics-invariance. The
-- derived merges' Legacy-subkey rule (D4/D9a) makes the two regimes agree
-- under every merge routing. tag/tx_created/tx_invalidated project from the
-- v3 derived columns when present; Q2 synthesis (Bool, 0, TX_OPEN) remains
-- the v2 fallback. Consequence, pre-registered: the P2 lsm test
-- edge_provenance_is_path_independent_after_reassert (two AUTHORS re-asserting
-- one edge via assert_batch) pins the P2 collapse and is UPDATED to expect
-- two coexisting assertions (path-independently); the 12 differential pairs
-- (all legacy-written v2 fixtures + the commutativity square) stay green
-- UNCHANGED.

-- D9 (compaction ⊕ rekey — §3.2 normative blocker).
-- merge_node_segments_derived / merge_edge_segments_derived rekey their fold:
--   record from a v2 segment            → Legacy(record_key)        (collapse,
--     newest-wins — identical to the base merge under both routings),
--   record from a v3 segment            → Assertion(record_key,
--     _source: Option<String>, rule_ast_hash: u32, tick) with tick =
--     _generation (metadata) falling back to ProvenanceV2.generation.
-- ⊕ (fold_tags) applies ONLY within one key = one aid; across different aids
-- records are BOTH kept. Output sorted deterministically by (record_key,
-- assertion key). fold_tags itself (E-FMT-001/002/003, E-TAG-001 checked
-- arithmetic) is unchanged. Base v2 merges untouched.
-- D9a consequence, pre-registered: the three merge.rs unit tests that pin the
-- record-key fold across DIFFERENT provenance generations
-- (derived_merge_folds_count_tags_not_dedup, derived_merge_round_trips_through_writer,
-- derived_edge_merge_folds_count_tags) encode exactly the fold §3.2 calls
-- «блокер, а не косметика» and are UPDATED: different (rule, generation) →
-- both records survive with separate tags; a same-aid duplicate still folds.
-- Any OTHER test that turns out to pin cross-aid folding will be listed in
-- round-010 with the same justification or, if it guards real engine
-- behavior the fact model must serve, will force a re-scope — not a silent
-- expectation edit.

-- D10 (§5.5 ByAttr in the base-five vocabulary). The doc's ByAttr{pred: file}
-- names the 141-vocabulary file/1 predicate, which does not exist until P6.
-- P4 encoding: SubjectSet::ByAttr { pred, values } is accepted iff pred is the
-- base `attr` predicate and values = [Str(key), matched values…] (first
-- element = the attribute key); ByAttr{attr, ["file", …changedFiles]}
-- reproduces today's reanalysis contract exactly. Any other pred →
-- E-CAP-001 (the per-attribute predicates are P6 vocabulary). Subject of a
-- fact row for scope matching = column 0, EXCEPT incoming where it is column
-- 1 (the edge source — incoming is edge's declared reverse view, and §5.5
-- scopes reproduce record areas in P4). Victims are enumerated from LIVE rows
-- only (a dead assertion cannot be re-superseded).

-- D11 (E-SUP-001 first arm — tick boundary). supersede(scope, at_tick)
-- requires at_tick STRICTLY greater than every victim assertion's tick;
-- violation aborts the WHOLE operation pre-commit (typed E-SUP-001, store
-- byte-identical by sha). The same boundary guards direct assert_batch writes
-- into the reserved supersedes predicate (D12): the referenced victim aid must
-- resolve to a known (live or dead) assertion in the pre-commit snapshot —
-- an UNRESOLVABLE victim aid is E-SUP-001 (monotonicity unprovable) — and
-- batch.tick must be strictly greater than the victim's tick. Well-foundedness:
-- ticks strictly decrease along supersedes chains, so supersedes(x,y) +
-- supersedes(y,x) is unconstructible through the boundary.

-- D12 (direct supersedes asserts). FactGroup gains a Supersedes { fact:
-- GroupFact } variant (additive enum extension): arity-2 Id×Id tuple over the
-- reserved supersedes predicate, subject to D11's boundary, persisted per D1.
-- Node/Edge groups still reject the supersedes predicate id
-- (record-vocabulary), and node groups reject the reserved node_type (D1).

-- D13 (supersedes PredicateDecl / planner integration — spec contract (8)).
-- catalog.rs gains a canonical `supersedes_decl()` (Adjacency, arity 2,
-- key_cols [0,1], reverse [1,0] — §2.4 "Adjacency с обратным раном по c1",
-- Bool semiring, MultiValued, Timeless). It is declared by LsmFactStore at
-- construction into the store's own catalog — NOT added to
-- with_base_relations: the with_base_relations id-space and base_names
-- dispatch are pinned by plan_golden (40,816 fingerprints bit-identical) and
-- by exec's storage dispatch, which has no supersedes service until P6/P7.
-- The §10.4 rationale «стоимость anti-join'а не попадает в план» is claimed
-- at the seam P3 built: (i) LsmFactStore::stats(supersedes) returns REAL
-- live_facts/live_asserts; (ii) a probe proves base_estimate (plan.rs:1305)
-- costs the supersedes decl+stats generically (catalog-driven, no name
-- special-case); (iii) a program with a negated supersedes leg registers and
-- plans WITHOUT the unknown-predicate E-CAT-002 path (§3.1 body-only default
-- rule; E-CAT-002 scope per round-009-pre H3 unchanged). derive/plan.rs
-- production code: ZERO changes expected (claim verified by plan_golden).

-- D14 (liveness algorithm — §2.4 definitional recursion). The superseded-aid
-- set of a snapshot is computed over the supersedes assertion set by
-- decreasing (tick, aid) order: an assertion of a supersedes fact is live iff
-- its own aid has not been claimed by an already-live higher-tick supersedes
-- assertion; victims of live supersedes assertions form the killed set.
-- Well-founded by D11 (superseder tick strictly exceeds victim tick).
-- live_filter = rule 1 (tx_invalidated may only CONFIRM death, D3 aborts a
-- lone cache-death) + anti-join against the killed set; fact live ⟺ ≥1 live
-- assertion. canonical_state_sha uses the SAME liveness (§9.1) and now
-- serializes |live assertions| per fact with assertions sorted by
-- (author-rank, tick) — the multi-assertion case P2's Q8 left to P4; C3
-- becomes CLAIMABLE and IS claimed (§10.5 C3 tag_fold arm).

-- D15 (read-path guard). The live_filter sole-read-path guard is the
-- grep-level hygiene test (facts::mod hygiene precedent): outside src/facts/,
-- ZERO consumers of the FactStore read surface exist (the only permitted
-- foreign reference is the SortOrder type import in derive/{catalog,plan,exec}
-- — a dispatch KEY type, not a read path); the test walks src/, skips
-- src/facts/, and fails listing offenders on any use of the facts store type
-- or its read methods. Inside facts/, live_filter and canonical_state_sha are
-- the only liveness authorities; raw sorted_run/prefix_scan remain the
-- documented physical runs (pair-8 discipline).

-- D16 (perspective discipline). supersede() with a non-main perspective is
-- E-CAP-001 "perspectives" (same §10.1 gate as assert_batch: today's record
-- format cannot represent one, so no scope can address one).

-- ── Hypotheses (round-010 verifies each; expected-vs-found) ─────────

-- H1 (C3 reconciliation gate — REQUIRED, claims doc §10.5 C3): one fact with
-- Count semiring asserted by TWO authors (derived-path fixture) → FullMerge
-- compact() → |live assertions| == 2 (not folded), canonical_state_sha
-- byte-identical before/after, and cross-process (subprocess helper precedent
-- facts::differential::state_sha_deterministic_across_two_processes).

-- H2 (E-SUP-001 both arms): (a) tick boundary per D11 — supersede at
-- at_tick ≤ victim tick → typed E-SUP-001, sha unchanged; direct supersedes
-- assert violating monotonicity or naming an unresolvable victim → E-SUP-001;
-- cycle unconstructible. (b) divergence — a snapshot where an assertion is
-- cache-dead with no live supersedes(_, aid) → live_filter AND
-- canonical_state_sha abort with "E-SUP-001" (contractual panic, D3).

-- H3 (author scope absolute, §4.2): A and B assert one fid; A supersedes All
-- → the fact stays live with exactly B's assertion; no SupersedeScope naming
-- A can kill B's assertion, including over conflicting Functional fids (two
-- live conflicting Functional assertions are LEGAL in P4 — arbitration is
-- P5); ByAttr{attr, ["file", changedFiles]} kills exactly A's assertions on
-- subjects in the changed files.

-- H4 (recursive liveness): superseding the supersede-assertion itself at a
-- higher tick resurrects the originally-superseded assertion; re-assert after
-- supersession at a higher tick = new aid, fact live.

-- H5 (equivalence): the 12 P2 differential pairs green UNCHANGED (handcrafted,
-- generated 2000/5000, survive-compaction, edge-reassert, tombstone+readd,
-- §2.3 conflict class, commutativity square, cross-process sha, perspective
-- floor, real-base ignored variant unchanged in code); NEW post-supersession
-- pairs: live_filter drops exactly the victim assertions; legacy-view
-- visibility of reserved records matches D1 (node-fact count == node_count_at
-- − reserved count; zero attr/type leakage).

-- H6 (planner/stats): stats(supersedes) real; plan_golden 40,816 bit-identical
